Hello,

I've recently run into some difficulty with large data sets (>5000 individuals with 14 microsatellite loci) when attempting to run AMOVAs using the poppr.amova() function. I'm curious if there are limits to the number of individuals or the size of the genind object that this function is capable of handling? These same data sets are processed in Arlequin rather quickly so it's puzzling to me why R/poppr/ade4 appear to be struggling and throwing errors related to long vectors and requiring RAM availability >40GB. If you have any thoughts on what might be causing this problem or how to troubleshoot the issue, I'd very much appreciate your advice. Thanks!

